+### VI.6 The CCNOT tape
+
+The prelude holds one stateful source of values: a CCNOT tape. It is wiring 1 of moop's tape, a mechanism of another language, admitted as an answer built from what Selvage already has. It is not a new mechanism and not on the execution path.
+
+```selvage
+type Tapes(a: Array(Bit), b: Array(Bit), i: I64, j: I64)
+
+rule tape_tick takes Tapes returns Tapes
+    Tapes(a, b, i, j) <-> Tapes(a, b, ni, nj) where
+        add a[i] * b[j] to a[(i + 1) mod length(a)]
+        add a[i] * b[j] to b[(j + length(b) - 1) mod length(b)]
+        ni is (i + 1) mod length(a)
+        i was (ni + length(a) - 1) mod length(a)
+        nj is (j + length(b) - 1) mod length(b)
+        j was (nj + 1) mod length(b)
+
+request Draw
+    draw() returns Bit
+    birth() returns CcnotTape
+
+answer CcnotTape for Draw takes Tapes
+    (draw(), s) <-> (seen, s) where
+        s is tape_tick(s)
+        seen is s.a[s.i]
+    (birth(), s) <-> (child, s) where
+        ca is array(Bit, length(s.a))
+        cb is array(Bit, length(s.b))
+        repeat with k from 0 to length(ca) - 1
+            s is tape_tick(s)
+            add s.a[s.i] to ca[k]
+        repeat with k from 0 to length(cb) - 1
+            s is tape_tick(s)
+            add s.a[s.i] to cb[k]
+        child is CcnotTape from Tapes(ca, cb, 0, 0)
+```
+
+- **The tape.** Two circular tapes of bits, `a` and `b`, under heads `i` and `j`. One tick (`tape_tick`) fires two CCNOTs that share their controls, the cells under both heads, and target the next cell of each tape; then `i` moves forward and `j` backward. Each update is `add a[i] * b[j] to …`, which is `ccnot` (VII.6), so the tick's bit updates are realized gate for gate.
+- **A draw is a deterministic observation** (C1). `draw` ticks the tape and copies the cell then under `i`. The copy goes into an empty name, so the answer is an embedding: nothing is kept, and `undo` refuses a draw the tape did not give. A draw is not a random bit, and nothing here claims statistical independence: on tapes of 8 and 13 cells a draw agrees with the draw 8 places back 74.8% of the time. A program that needs random numbers does not use `draw`. `Draw` is the tape's request; it is not a general interface for generators. Another generator, such as a certified rule over words, is a rule of its own, never another implementation of the tape.
+- **A birth** draws one cell for each cell of a child tape, `a`'s cells first, and gives the child as a new tape. It is certified: the parent advances by ticks and the child is copies, so taking a birth back gives the parent back. A birth promises a valid reversible initialization and no more; how many different children a tape can bear is not part of it (on tapes of 8 and 13 cells, 2.80% of possible children).
+- **A program makes its tape** (C3). `CcnotTape from Tapes(a, b, 0, 0)` makes one from tapes the program fills; it chooses which tape it uses and where it goes. No tape is ambient: `ask draw()` with no tape installed is refused at Root. The tapes a program starts from are an explicit initialization, not a source of entropy, and seeding does not make the tape random.
+- **Domain.** Each tape needs at least two cells, or a target would be a control, and each head must be inside its tape. No type states that, so R4 and bounds checks guard it when the tape runs: an empty tape is refused by a division by zero, a one-cell tape by R4. `selvage check` reports the tick, the draw and the birth as one-to-one, with nothing more established (V.2).
+- **Moop's trace.** The tape is pinned to moop's own implementation: `tests/programs/ccnot_tape.selv` prints `tests/programs/ccnot_tape.trace` byte for byte, a trace moop's C implementation also prints. A change of wiring is a new wiring with a new trace, never an edit.
+- **Admission** (I.4). *Foundation:* an answer (Tier 4) over bit updates (Tier 1). *Synergy:* it gives Request generation, a certified birth that is taken back, and it gives the realization lineage an answer whose defining step is `ccnot` itself, a first program for the reversible profile (IX.4). It makes nothing unnecessary; of the four steps this is the weakest. *Interference:* six names are reserved; no example, test program or benchmark changes. *Uniformity:* only existing constructs, with the domain guarded by the existing checks. The decisions taken in admitting it are C1 to C4 (XII.6).
