+rule tape_tick takes Tapes returns Tapes
+    Tapes(a, b, i, j) <-> Tapes(a, b, ni, nj) where
+        add a[i] * b[j] to a[(i + 1) mod length(a)]
+        add a[i] * b[j] to b[(j + length(b) - 1) mod length(b)]
+        ni is (i + 1) mod length(a)
+        i was (ni + length(a) - 1) mod length(a)
+        nj is (j + length(b) - 1) mod length(b)
+        j was (nj + 1) mod length(b)
+
+# A draw ticks the tape and copies the cell then under head i: a deterministic observation of the
+# tape, not a random bit.  A birth draws one cell for each cell of a child tape, a's first.  The
+# tape a program draws from is the one it makes, from a seed it chooses; a seed is where the tape
+# starts, not a source of entropy.
+request Draw
+    draw() returns Bit
+    birth() returns CcnotTape
+
+answer CcnotTape for Draw takes Tapes
+    (draw(), s) <-> (seen, s) where
+        s is tape_tick(s)
+        seen is s.a[s.i]
+    (birth(), s) <-> (child, s) where
+        ca is array(Bit, length(s.a))
+        cb is array(Bit, length(s.b))
+        repeat with k from 0 to length(ca) - 1
+            s is tape_tick(s)
+            add s.a[s.i] to ca[k]
+        repeat with k from 0 to length(cb) - 1
+            s is tape_tick(s)
+            add s.a[s.i] to cb[k]
+        child is CcnotTape from Tapes(ca, cb, 0, 0)
